## Upstream dataset material

Question text, source annotations, captions, and other material
originating from upstream datasets are excluded from the QIMG-7
CC BY 4.0 grant and retain their applicable source licenses and notices:

| QIMG-7 subset | Upstream source and applicable terms |
|---|---|
| AlpacaFact | Derived from AlpacaFarm; CC BY-NC 4.0 |
| LongFact | CC BY 4.0 for non-software materials |
| FAVA | CC BY 4.0 |
| Biography | Originates from the MIT-licensed FActScore repository; any associated third-party material retains its original terms |

Because the bundle contains AlpacaFact-derived material, the complete
QIMG-7 dataset must not be represented as wholly CC BY 4.0 or as
permitting unrestricted commercial reuse. Separable components remain
available under their respective licenses. See LICENSE-DATA for source
links, attribution information, and further details.

## Images

This repository does not redistribute source images or their polluted
variants except where the applicable source terms permit. For other
image items, we release the source URL, a content hash, the manipulation
prompt, and, where available, a reconstruction script. Availability of
these materials does not itself grant permission to download, reproduce,
modify, or redistribute the underlying image.

Any included image files remain subject to the copyrights, licenses,
website terms, and other rights of their respective sources, identified
where available by `original_image_url`. Public availability does not
imply permission for reuse.

## Content notice

Polluted items in this repository contain deliberately false statements,
including statements about real named people and organizations. They are
synthetic benchmark artifacts for robustness research and are not
factual claims. They are not intended to be extracted, republished, or
indexed as factual content.

## Archive-level metadata

Where a distribution platform supports a mixed-license or `other`
identifier, that identifier should be used. If a platform requires one
standard license identifier and provides no mixed-license option,
CC BY-NC 4.0 may be used as a conservative package-level identifier,
provided that this mixed-license notice is retained. The package-level
identifier does not relicense, restrict, or override separately licensed
or excluded third-party material.

## Attribution

When sharing material covered by the QIMG-7 CC BY 4.0 license, users
must retain the supplied creator identification, copyright notice,
license notice and link, source link where reasonably practicable, and
an indication of any modifications. Users must also comply separately
with the attribution and notice requirements of applicable upstream
licenses.

For academic use, please cite the QIMG-7 paper using the citation
provided in CITATION.cff or the README.

This notice clarifies the scope of the repository's licenses. It does
not revoke or alter licenses validly granted for earlier versions.